message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: "Algebraic ratios between exact prime-race crossings"
abstract: "Of 1,891 pairs of signed hits through one million, at least 1,830 have transcendental height quotient. On 547/727 there are at least 349 inequivalent hits before exp(1000) and at least 9,821 signed hits before exp(12500). Under Dirichlet GRH at most three hits of magnitude 1.9735 share algebraic ratios at any heights, and the latter finite range contains at least 3,274 classes."
